        <enumvalue id="classllvm_1_1_v_p_lane_1afb4648a83781e7ee62f34771ea338c29a7fb55ed0b7a30342ba6da306428cae04" prot="public">
          <name>First</name>
          <briefdescription>
<para>For First, Lane is the index into the first N elements of a fixed-vector &lt;N x &lt;ElTy&gt;&gt; or a scalable vector &lt;vscale x N x &lt;ElTy&gt;&gt;. </para>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="classllvm_1_1_v_p_lane_1afb4648a83781e7ee62f34771ea338c29a69d68d161f986e83192f701108a729bc" prot="public">
          <name>ScalableLast</name>
          <briefdescription>
<para>For ScalableLast, Lane is the offset from the start of the last N-element subvector in a scalable vector &lt;vscale x N x &lt;ElTy&gt;&gt;. </para>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>For example, a Lane of 0 corresponds to lane <computeroutput>(vscale - 1) * N</computeroutput>, a Lane of 1 corresponds to <computeroutput>((vscale - 1) * N) + 1</computeroutput>, etc. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_v_p_lane_1afb4648a83781e7ee62f34771ea338c29" kindref="member">Kind</ref> describes how to interpret Lane. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
        </detaileddescription>
